    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly presents this superb two-bedroom corner apartment enjoying a bright south-east facing aspect, B energy rating, two private balconies and designated parking in this mature and well-managed Dublin 2 development next to Grand Canal Dock. Positioned on the third floor, No. 26 benefits from a desirable dual aspect which floods the interior with natural light, while its outlook over the quiet internal courtyard provides an excellent sense of privacy despite the exceptionally central location.\r\n\r\nThe bright and spacious open-plan kitchen, living and dining room is the heart of the apartment, with direct access to both balconies providing valuable outdoor space and an attractive outlook over the residents' courtyard. The fully fitted kitchen features excellent storage, integrated appliances, and an L-shaped peninsula which creates a natural divide between the kitchen and living areas.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation also comprises a welcoming entrance hall with excellent storage, including a cleverly concealed washing machine, two generous double bedrooms with built-in wardrobes and a well-appointed main bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe combination of its corner position, south-east orientation and two balconies gives the apartment a particularly bright and airy feel. Further benefits include a designated parking space and access to the attractive landscaped residents' courtyard.\r\n\r\nMore about the location…\r\n\r\nThe location is exceptional, tucked away just off Sir John Rogerson's Quay and only a five-minute walk from Grand Canal Dock. Trinity College, the IFSC and Dublin city centre are all within easy walking distance, making this an ideal base from which to enjoy city living.\r\n\r\nThe Docklands offers an outstanding selection of cafés, restaurants, bars, gyms and shops, alongside landmark amenities including The Marker Hotel and Bord Gáis Energy Theatre. Excellent transport connections are also close at hand, including DART, Luas and numerous bus services.\r\n\r\nA bright, private and exceptionally well-located city apartment offering two double bedrooms, two balconies and designated parking in the heart of Dublin's Docklands. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hallway (4.32m x 3.15m)\r\nWith an intercom, oak style laminate flooring and hot press with water tank & built in sliding wardrobe with washing machine.\r\n\r\nBathroom (2.27m x 1.76m)\r\nFully tiled with white three piece suite including an enclosed shower cubicle, wash hand basin and WC.\r\n\r\nKitchen/living/dining room (7.46m x 6.21m)\r\nSouth-east facing with courtyard views, oak-style laminate flooring, decorative fireplace, and access to two balconies. Fully fitted kitchen with L-shaped peninsula, navy cabinetry, tiled splashback, integrated oven, four-ring electric hob, extractor fan, fridge/freezer and dishwasher.\r\n\r\nBalcony 1 (2.92m x 1.27m)\r\nEast facing with artificial grass.\r\n\r\nBalcony 2 (1.69m x 1.19m)\r\nSouth facing with tiled flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (4.96m x 2.38m)\r\nSouth facing double bedroom with fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (4.25m x 2.40m)\r\nSouth facing double bedroom with fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nAll measurements are approximate and for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Third floor two-bedroom apartment.\r\nDesirable corner position offering excellent privacy.\r\nB energy rating.\r\nSouth-east facing aspect.\r\nBright open-plan kitchen/living/dining room.\r\nTwo private balconies overlooking the quiet internal courtyard.\r\nTwo generous double bedrooms with built-in wardrobes.\r\nExcellent hallway storage with concealed washing machine.\r\nDesignated car parking space.\r\nAttractive residents’ courtyard.\r\nMature and well-managed development.\r\nApproximately five minutes’ walk from Grand Canal Dock.\r\nExcellent transport links with DART and Luas nearby."
      },
      {
